  <presentation id="composable-ai">
    <title short="Composable Architecture for AI Systems">Composable Architecture for AI Systems: APIs, MCP, Skills, Sub-Agents, and Workflows</title>
    <date short="2026-08-20">August 20, 2026</date>
    <toc class="abstract">AI is a powerful tool, but it is not the only tool, and most systems worth building are hybrids of AI and non-AI parts. That line between them doesn't sit neatly between domains. It runs inside every domain, and it should move as you learn. This talk looks at the mechanisms for connecting across that line: APIs, MCP, agent skills, and sub-agents, as well as at workflows as a way to move the line itself: when an agent keeps rediscovering the same business process, that process belongs in deterministic execution, not in a prompt. You'll leave knowing which mechanism belongs where, and how to keep shifting work out of AI as your system settles.</toc>
    <slide id="agent-erik">
      <title>Erik Wilde</title>
      <img src="OAI-logo.png" title="OpenAPI Initiative" href="https://www.openapis.org/" style="float: right ; clear : both ; width : 30% ; margin : 0% 4% 4% 4% ; "/>
      <ul>
        <li>Ambassador for the <a href="https://www.openapis.org/">OpenAPI Initiative (OAI)</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/erikwilde"><img src="linkedin-logo.png" style=" height : 1em ; "/> <code>linkedin.com/in/erikwilde</code></a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/ErikWilde"><img src="youtube-logo.png" style=" height : 1em ; "/> <code>youtube.com/ErikWilde</code></a></li>
      </ul>
    </slide>
    <part id="ai-engineering">
      <title>AI Engineering is Growing Up</title>
      <slide id="ai-power">
        <title>A Trillion Operations for 2 + 3?</title>
        <img src="ai-hammer.png" title="Maslow's AI Hammer" style="float: right ; height : 70% ; margin : 0% 4% 4% 4% ; "/>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ;"></th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ;">Machine Instructions</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ;">AI</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">Elapsed time</td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~1 nanosecond</td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~0.1–2 seconds</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">Computation</td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~1 integer operation</td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~10<sup>11</sup>–10<sup>13</sup> arithmetic operations</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">Energy</td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~10–100 picojoules</td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ;">~10–1,000 joules</td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li>Billion times slower</li>
          <li>Trillion times more computation</li>
          <li>10<sup>12</sup>–10<sup>14</sup> times more energy</li>
          <li>And no guarantee it got the answer right</li>
        </ul>
      </slide>
      <slide id="pitch-vs-reality">
        <title>The Benevolent AI Superintelligence?</title>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ; width : 90% ; margin : 0 5% ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Perfect Vision</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Current Reality</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>One agent, one model, all tasks</li>
                <li>Always gets the right answer</li>
                <li>Autonomous, self-directing</li>
                <li>No human engineering required</li>
                <li><q>Just describe what you want</q> and trust us</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Same prompt returns different answers</li>
                <li>Behavior drift on model updates</li>
                <li>Most business logic is deterministic</li>
                <li>AI earns its keep on judgment tasks</li>
                <li>Reliability = clean cuts between the two</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </slide>
      <slide id="design-vs-runtime">
        <title>AI at Design Time! AI at Runtime?</title>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ; width : 90% ; margin : 0 5% ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">AI at Design Time</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">AI at Runtime</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Recognizes patterns</li>
                <li>Writes the code</li>
                <li>You review and ship</li>
                <li>Runs deterministically forever after</li>
                <li>Use it aggressively</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>The only tool for genuine judgment tasks</li>
                <li>The only tool for unstructured input at scale</li>
                <li>Real value where no non-AI option exists</li>
                <li>Costly per call — budget deliberately</li>
                <li>Handle with care</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
      </slide>
    </part>
    <part id="where-the-line-runs">
      <title>Where the Line Runs</title>
      <slide id="boundary-history">
        <title>The Boundary Has a History</title>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ; width : 90% ; margin : 0 5% ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 33% ;">Before Machine Learning</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 33% ;">Machine Learning</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 33% ;">Generative AI</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>No boundary at all</li>
                <li>Everything is code</li>
                <li>If code could not do it, you did not build it</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>The boundary appears</li>
                <li>Probabilistic components are possible but expensive</li>
                <li>So you keep them small and deliberate</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>The cost collapses</li>
                <li>The boundary moves a long way, fast</li>
                <li>Often without anyone deciding that it should</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li>The boundary sits where the economics put it</li>
          <li>Generative AI changed the price, not the principle</li>
        </ul>
      </slide>
      <slide id="domains-and-interfaces">
        <title>It's Software Architecture</title>
        <ul>
          <li>Macro architecture: domains and the interfaces between them remain unchanged</li>
          <li>The AI / non-AI line is <em>not</em> a domain boundary</li>
          <li>It runs <em>inside</em> every domain: judgment work and deterministic work, side by side</li>
          <li>Micro architecture: where that line sits, and which mechanism crosses it</li>
          <li>The line may move because of new processes and workflows</li>
        </ul>
      </slide>
    </part>
    <part id="crossing-the-boundary">
      <title>Crossing the Boundary</title>
      <slide id="two-contracts">
        <title>Two Kinds of Component, Two Kinds of Contract</title>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ; width : 90% ; margin : 0 5% ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Deterministic</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Probabilistic</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Same input, same output</li>
                <li>Tested exhaustively, within reason</li>
                <li>Composes predictably</li>
                <li>Failure is exceptional</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Same input, a distribution of outputs</li>
                <li>Evaluated statistically</li>
                <li>Adapts to what it is given</li>
                <li>Variation is expected</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li>From here on: <em>probabilistic</em> and <em>deterministic</em>, not <q>AI</q> and <q>non-AI</q></li>
        </ul>
      </slide>
      <slide id="two-crossings">
        <title>Crossing the Boundary Changes Your Guarantees</title>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ; width : 90% ; margin : 0 5% ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Deterministic &#8594; Probabilistic</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Probabilistic &#8594; Deterministic</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>You delegate judgment</li>
                <li>You give up repeatability</li>
                <li>The uncertainty is in the answer</li>
                <li>Managed with evals: statistical, after the fact</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>You delegate execution</li>
                <li>You give up guaranteed invocation</li>
                <li>The uncertainty is in whether the call happens at all</li>
                <li>Managed by removing discretion where discretion no longer adds value</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li>Bottom line: the two directions are not symmetric, and neither are their fixes</li>
        </ul>
      </slide>
    </part>
    <part id="mechanisms">
      <title>What to Use When</title>
      <slide id="mcp">
        <title>Model Context Protocol (MCP)</title>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ; width : 90% ; margin : 0 5% ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Use for</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Not for</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Letting an LLM reach any external capability</li>
                <li>Exposing your APIs, databases, workflows as tools</li>
                <li>Deterministic operations the LLM should invoke on demand</li>
                <li>The default answer for <q>how do I connect the LLM to X?</q></li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Packaging prompt patterns (that's skills)</li>
                <li>Complex multi-step business processes (wrap a workflow instead)</li>
                <li>Delegating whole reasoning tasks (that's sub-agents)</li>
                <li>Anywhere you need guaranteed invocation (LLM decides when to call)</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li>Bottom line: ...</li>
        </ul>
      </slide>
      <slide id="skills">
        <title>Skills</title>
        <table style="border-collapse: collapse ; border: 2px solid #000000 ; width : 90% ; margin : 0 5% ;">
          <tr>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Use for</th>
            <th style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; background: #eeeeee ; width : 50% ;">Not for</th>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Packaging a prompt pattern you keep re-typing</li>
                <li>Sharing a way of working across sessions and projects</li>
                <li>Loading context (style guides, docs) on demand</li>
                <li>Composing MCP tool usage into a reusable recipe</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 2px solid #000000 ; padding: 10px 20px ; vertical-align : top ;">
              <ul>
                <li>Reliable business processes (workflows do this better)</li>
                <li>Behavior that must run identically each time</li>
                <li>Anything that needs versioning or auditability</li>
                <li>Delegating to a different model (sub-agents)</li>
              </ul>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>
        <ul>
          <li>Bottom line: ...</li>
        </ul>
      </slide>
    </part>
